Sorting Algorithm Analyzer is a terminal-based application built in C to practically evaluate algorithmic efficiency and data manipulation. Operating directly through the Windows shell, the program implements and compares Merge Sort and Insertion Sort to demonstrate algorithmic optimization.

The project highlights the real-world performance trade-offs between different time complexities, leveraging Merge Sort's O(nlogn) efficiency for large, randomized datasets, and Insertion Sort's low overhead for smaller or nearly-sorted arrays.
